    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town hosted the first Latter Day Saint temple, completed in 1836, making it the movement's early headquarters from 1831‑1837.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        26,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirtland%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the 1836 Kirtland Temple dedication, attendees reported heavenly visions, a dramatic moment in early Mormon history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirtland%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Historic Kirtland Village, opened in 2000, recreates 1830s life with replicas of a schoolhouse, sawmill, and ashery.",
